WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:07.490
The next day Aunt Polly told Pollyanna that a new doctor had been summoned.

2
00:00:07.491 --> 00:00:15.129
"Another doctor—besides Dr. Warren—might know of a treatment to help you get well faster."

3
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.065
Pollyanna's face lit up with joy.

4
00:00:18.066 --> 00:00:24.211
"Dr. Chilton! Oh, Aunt Polly, I've wanted him to visit ever since my accident.

5
00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:29.889
But I was afraid you wouldn't allow that because he saw you with the rose in your hair."

6
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.647
Aunt Polly's face turned white, then red, then back to white again.

7
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:38.621
She struggled to keep her voice cheerful.

8
00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:43.335
"Oh, no, dear! I didn't mean Dr. Chilton.

9
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:48.980
This new doctor, Dr. Mead, is a very famous one from New York.

10
00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:52.971
He knows a great deal about injuries like yours."

11
00:00:52.972 --> 00:01:00.157
Pollyanna's face fell. "I can't believe he knows half as much as Dr. Chilton.

12
00:01:00.158 --> 00:01:04.326
After all, Dr. Chilton treated Mr. Pendleton's broken leg.

13
00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:09.873
If you don't mind, I'd prefer to have Dr. Chilton."

14
00:01:09.874 --> 00:01:16.552
"But I do mind." Aunt Polly straightened Pollyanna's covers.

15
00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:19.682
"I'd do almost anything for you, dear.

16
00:01:19.683 --> 00:01:24.821
However, for reasons I can't discuss, I don't want Dr. Chilton here.

17
00:01:24.822 --> 00:01:31.114
Besides, he can't know as much as this doctor, who's a specialist."

18
00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:37.974
Pollyanna was not ready to give up. "But, Aunt Polly, if you loved Dr. Chilton—"

19
00:01:37.975 --> 00:01:42.334
"What did you say?" Aunt Polly looked startled.

20
00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:47.598
"If you loved Dr. Chilton instead of that New York doctor, you'd get better faster.

21
00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:54.400
I mean, if you were the patient, which you're not." Pollyanna sighed.

22
00:01:54.401 --> 00:02:02.309
"I'm just trying to say that I love Dr. Chilton, so he'd make me feel better faster if he came."

23
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.119
Aunt Polly looked relieved when the nurse entered the room.

24
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.886
"I'm sorry, Pollyanna," Aunt Polly said.

25
00:02:09.887 --> 00:02:13.987
"You must let me decide what's best for you this time.

26
00:02:13.988 --> 00:02:20.360
Besides, it's already arranged that the doctor will arrive tomorrow."

27
00:02:20.361 --> 00:02:25.926
As it happened, Dr. Mead did not arrive the next day.

28
00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:30.767
Aunt Polly received a telegram that he had suddenly taken ill.

29
00:02:30.768 --> 00:02:35.184
This led Pollyanna to plead again for Dr. Chilton.

30
00:02:35.185 --> 00:02:41.605
"It would be so easy for Dr. Chilton to come now," Pollyanna pointed out.

31
00:02:41.606 --> 00:02:51.092
Aunt Polly shook her head. "I'll give you anything you want but that, dear." ***

32
00:02:51.093 --> 00:03:00.549
As the days passed, Aunt Polly did everything she could to please Pollyanna—except summon Dr. Chilton.

33
00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:06.657
"I wouldn't have believed it, if I didn't see it with my own eyes," Nancy said to Tom.

34
00:03:06.658 --> 00:03:10.842
It was early one morning, and they were having breakfast in the kitchen.

35
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:14.910
"Miss Polly didn't used to allow the dog and cat upstairs.

36
00:03:14.911 --> 00:03:25.050
Now she lets Buffy and Fluffy tumble on the bed just because it makes Pollyanna happy."

37
00:03:25.051 --> 00:03:28.577
Tom chuckled as he sipped his coffee.

38
00:03:28.578 --> 00:03:37.345
Nancy went on. "When Miss Polly isn't sitting with Pollyanna, she's moving those prisms around to catch the sunlight.

39
00:03:37.346 --> 00:03:44.340
She sends for fresh flowers from a neighbor's greenhouse, and here's the most astonishing thing.

40
00:03:44.341 --> 00:03:51.901
The other day I caught the nurse fixing Miss Polly's hair while Pollyanna gave instructions.

41
00:03:51.902 --> 00:04:00.323
And Miss Polly has worn her hair that way every day just to please that child! She's actually almost—"

42
00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:03.903
"Pretty?" Tom finished her sentence.

43
00:04:03.904 --> 00:04:10.595
"I told you she used to be pretty. And I bet she doesn't look so old now."

44
00:04:10.596 --> 00:04:17.736
"That's right." Nancy went to the stove and brought Tom another pancake.

45
00:04:17.737 --> 00:04:23.721
"I still haven't figured out who Miss Polly was engaged to."

46
00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:31.268
"And you won't learn that from me!" Tom poured maple syrup on his pancake.

47
00:04:31.269 --> 00:04:34.978
"How is Pollyanna these days?"

48
00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:39.872
Nancy sighed. "There's no change.

49
00:04:39.873 --> 00:04:45.142
She just lies in bed and tries to be glad about something."

50
00:04:45.143 --> 00:04:55.539
Tom nodded. "From what I hear around town, Pollyanna has told everybody about that Glad Game her father invented."

51
00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:00.212
"Everybody but Miss Polly, who didn't want to hear anything about him.

52
00:05:00.213 --> 00:05:05.705
Pollyanna is always telling me how glad she'll be when she can go to school again.

53
00:05:05.706 --> 00:05:13.800
Or visit Mrs. Snow or Mr. Pendleton. Or ride in Dr. Chilton's carriage."

54
00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:17.445
Nancy stopped talking and studied her empty plate.

55
00:05:17.446 --> 00:05:21.347
When she looked up, her eyes were filled with tears.

56
00:05:21.348 --> 00:05:28.194
"Oh, Tom! Pollyanna doesn't realize how far in the future all this gladness is.

57
00:05:28.195 --> 00:05:33.862
And both Pollyanna and Miss Polly are getting so thin!"

58
00:05:33.863 --> 00:05:37.020
Tom drank one last swallow of coffee.

59
00:05:37.021 --> 00:05:44.850
"The sooner that New York doctor gets here, the better!"

